// Type-checks the test files that `tsconfig.json` excludes.
//
// Without this, no test file in this package was ever type-checked, and vitest
// does not type-check either. That gap is not cosmetic: a test can assert
// against a value whose type makes the assertion impossible, and it stays green
// because the annotation is stripped rather than evaluated. Verified by stub —
// widening a type a test asserted on left the assertion passing.
//
// Node types are scoped HERE and nowhere else. `tsconfig.json` pins
// `types: []` so that `@types/node`, which these tests need, cannot reach the
// browser components this package publishes.
//
// Every test file compiles today, so there is no opt-out list. If one is ever
// needed, it belongs here as a list that shrinks: removing an entry is an
// improvement, adding one is a regression worth arguing for in review.
//
// `rootDir` is widened to the package root and `scripts/**/*` added to `include`. The build
// scripts are TypeScript and the suites import them, so they have to be in the program — and
// `rootDir: "src"`, inherited from the shipping config, rejects any file outside `src` with
// TS6059. That constraint exists to shape EMIT, and this pass is `noEmit`, so widening it costs
// nothing and buys the scripts type-checking they never had as `.mjs` with hand-written
// declarations beside them.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "rootDir": ".",
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*", "scripts/**/*"],
  "exclude": ["dist", "node_modules"]
}
